  <h3 class="section-title">INTERNET / WEBSITE</h3>
  <ul style="margin-top: 10px;">
    <li>For the avoidance of doubt, the rates offered in this Agreement are not applicable for sale on Resort only (non-packaged) basis via online consumer channels including, but not limited to, the distributor's own, affiliate, partner or onward distributor's websites. It is the contracted distributor's responsibility to enforce this clause.</li>
    <li>Should these contract rates to be used via online consumer channels, the rates must be packaged with air tickets and or other services such as tours, spa and dining. If it stands alone there must be a minimum mark up of 35% to thereto.</li>
    <li>Request to sell via online consumer channels must be received and approved in writing by the Resort.</li>
    <li>The Resort reserves the right to cancel the contract if this condition is breached.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="section-title">BROCHURE COPY AND PHOTOGRAPHS</h3>
  <ul style="margin-top: 10px;">
    <li>All brochure copy and photographs produced by company depicting the Resort must be approved by the Resort in advance. The Resort will have 14 business days to review and approve the submitted brochure copy and photographs. In the event the Resort does not respond after 14 business days of receipt of the brochure copy and photographs, then such brochure copy and photographs will be deemed approved.</li>
    <li>In event company does not submit brochure copy and photographs and the Resort determines that the brochure copy and/or photographs contain incorrect information and misrepresents the Resort in any manner then all brochure contribution fund for that edition of the brochure will be reimbursed to the Resort.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="section-title">IMPOSSIBILITY OF PERFORMANCE</h3>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">It is expressly agreed that each party will be relieved of its obligation under this agreement in the event and to the extent that their ability to uphold their stated obligations is hampered or prevented by a cause reasonably beyond their control. This includes, without limitation, acts of God, change of statutes by the Indonesian Government, war, fire, flood or explosion, natural disaster, sale of the Resort, necessary and essential construction, arrest or seizure under legal process, strike or work stoppage.</p>

